":"FMG","position":{"start":{"line":157,"column":1},"end":{"line":157,"column":1}},"key":"EGrR4qBOsN"}],"key":"e1HQAxSxxN"},{"type":"tableCell","position":{"start":{"line":157,"column":1},"end":{"line":157,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":157,"column":1},"end":{"line":157,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"3","position":{"start":{"line":157,"column":1},"end":{"line":157,"column":1}},"key":"Dn53WZZDzG"}],"key":"Rheot677rO"}],"key":"UDGZ8tz8B3"},{"type":"tableCell","position":{"start":{"line":157,"column":1},"end":{"line":157,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"converged","position":{"start":{"line":157,"column":1},"end":{"line":157,"column":1}},"key":"P0iy08qgva"}],"key":"J19oUF1diP"},{"type":"tableCell","position":{"start":{"line":157,"column":1},"end":{"line":157,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":157,"column":1},"end":{"line":157,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"3.0 s","position":{"start":{"line":157,"column":1},"end":{"line":157,"column":1}},"key":"a5i4UhoPwT"}],"key":"P2vLOk8yox"}],"key":"tfbylNgFCS"}],"key":"JRZKbwbQby"}],"key":"AnYO7Tnz24"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":159,"column":1},"end":{"line":162,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"On the constant-viscosity problem both work. GAMG takes a few hundred\niterations of the velocity block against two, but the solve is a couple of\nseconds either way, and on a model that size the choice does not change the\nday.","position":{"start":{"line":159,"column":1},"end":{"line":159,"column":1}},"key":"dV8bHOEM5f"}],"key":"jxRhdkQ4OQ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":164,"column":1},"end":{"line":168,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"With a factor of 10⁴ across a viscous layer, GAMG does not converge the\nvelocity block at all: it runs into the iteration cap, at 200 and again at\n2000, and takes 78 seconds to fail. FMG takes three iterations and three\nseconds. The gap is not a speed-up, it is the difference between a model that\nruns and one that does not.","position":{"start":{"line":164,"column":1},"end":{"line":164,"column":1}},"key":"zIraFuV7xD"}],"key":"zcAORghGjv"},{"type":"admonition","kind":"note","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The GAMG here is the default configuration","position":{"start":{"line":170,"column":1},"end":{"line":170,"column":1}},"key":"frK6g8RB76"}],"key":"WFNaWzUUJh"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":171,"column":1},"end":{"line":175,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"These runs use the GAMG bundle Underworld applies without tuning. Algebraic\nmultigrid on an elasticity-like operator usually wants the near-null-space —\nthe rigid body modes — supplied to it, and it can be made considerably better\nthan this. The comparison shows what the two choices give you out of the box,\nwhich is the choice most people are actually making.","position":{"start":{"line":171,"column":1},"end":{"line":171,"column":1}},"key":"x3dopdywyE"}],"key":"GpZysbXNY6"}],"key":"Gpjw18XuEs"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":178,"column":1},"end":{"line":178,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using it","position":{"start":{"line":178,"column":1},"end":{"line":178,"column":1}},"key":"bsLgC8ApHY"}],"identifier":"using-it","label":"Using it","html_id":"using-it","implicit":true,"key":"JKLn4pt8FF"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","value":"# Build the hierarchy at mesh construction: base + two refinements.\nmesh = uw.meshing.UnstructuredSimplexBox(cellSize=0.05, refinement=2)\n\nstokes = uw.systems.Stokes(mesh)\nstokes.preconditioner = \"auto\"        # FMG when a hierarchy exists\nstokes.solve()\n\nprint(len(mesh.dm_hierarchy))         # how many levels there are\nprint(stokes.preconditioner_settings) # what was applied\nprint(stokes.pc_fallbacks)            # anything declined, and why","position":{"start":{"line":180,"column":1},"end":{"line":191,"column":1}},"key":"gnkNVoBvDK"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":193,"column":1},"end":{"line":195,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"If a solve is slow and the mesh has no hierarchy, that is the first thing to\nchange: rebuild the mesh with ","position":{"start":{"line":193,"column":1},"end":{"line":193,"column":1}},"key":"jvx98NLOpm"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"refinement","position":{"start":{"line":193,"column":1},"end":{"line":193,"column":1}},"key":"fkyOt1WQdI"},{"type":"text","value":" rather than at a fine ","position":{"start":{"line":193,"column":1},"end":{"line":193,"column":1}},"key":"Enp3sm1nSJ"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cellSize","position":{"start":{"line":193,"column":1},"end":{"line":193,"column":1}},"key":"WR8KLBCEo5"},{"type":"text","value":",\nand the same resolution arrives with the coarse levels attached.","position":{"start":{"line":193,"column":1},"end":{"line":193,"column":1}},"key":"Y2PhtO0nKU"}],"key":"QmnBhCmutm"},{"type":"div","class":"uwtn-discuss","children":[{"type":"div","class":"uwtn-discuss-head","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Comments","key":"zmHJZIPDAm"}],"key":"TQs5i0IB8v"},{"type":"div","class":"uwtn-discuss-body","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Discussion of these notes happens in GitHub Discussions, so it stays with the source and is searchable alongside it.","key":"mbPBRAm4QV"}],"key":"EL9aJv1kKj"},{"type":"div","class":"uwtn-discuss-links","children":[{"type":"link","url":"https://github.com/Underworld-Technical-Notes/underworldcode.org/discussions?discussions_q=setting-up-full-multigrid","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read the discussion","key":"LQh00eVRLo"}],"urlSource":"https://github.com/Underworld-Technical-Notes/underworldcode.org/discussions?discussions_q=setting-up-full-multigrid","error":true,"key":"mjNltTmoz3"},{"type":"link","url":"https://github.com/Underworld-Technical-Notes/underworldcode.org/discussions/new?category=